EXECTST.COM - a DOS program starting a DOS program
    OK   shrank to our own size, so there is room for a child
  running ARGS.COM 5 as a child:
ARGS.COM - what a 16-bit program was handed:
  tail  [ 5]
  AX    0000
  FCB1  00 [           ]
  FCB2  00 [           ]
  env   0626
    COMSPEC=C:\COMMAND.COM
    PATH=C:\TESTS;C:\
  path  C:\TESTS\ARGS.COM
    OK   control came back to us
  4Dh says (type/code) 00/05
    OK   the child exited 5, normally
    OK   a second 4Dh reports nothing, as DOS does
    OK   a child that does not exist fails with error 2
    OK   4B03h loaded ARGS.COM into a block of ours, byte for byte
    OK   4B03h at segment 0 is refused, not loaded over the vectors
  and four levels deep, to test the nesting stack:
    level 3
    level 2
    level 1
    level 0
    OK   the bottom level's code came all the way back up
EXECTST done
